Seed face photos — provenance and terms
=======================================

These face crops are used only to seed the ITAP demo database (`pnpm seed`). They were produced by
`apps/backend/src/seed/tools/extract-faces.ts`; `manifest.json` lists the exact frame or bounding box of every crop.

All people shown are real. In the demo every one of them is given a FICTIONAL name, company, job title, role and
history (generated by `src/seed/peoplePlan.ts`). No real identity, employment, conduct or watch-list status is
implied. The "watch-list" persona (person-02) is a demo role only, with a neutral note; nothing about the person in
the photo is suggested.

Sources
-------

person-01, person-02 (2 crops each)
  Frames of `docker/stream-server/videos/warehouse.mp4`, a Pexels stock video.
  Pexels License (https://www.pexels.com/license/): free to use, modification allowed, no attribution required.
  The Pexels licence does not allow portraying identifiable people in an offensive or misleading way; hence the
  fictional, neutral personas above.

person-03 (4 crops)
  Frames of `docker/stream-server/videos/serverroom.mp4`, a Pexels stock video. Same licence and conditions.

person-04 … person-10 (1 crop each)
  Crops of `libs/InsightFace-REST/misc/test_images/lumia.jpg`, a test image shipped with the InsightFace-REST
  repository (git submodule). The repository's Apache-2.0 licence covers its source code; it does not establish
  who holds the rights to this photograph or whether the people in it consented to redistribution. Photo rights
  are therefore UNCERTAIN. Use for local demos and tests only; replace these crops with licensed or synthetic
  faces before any public distribution of the seed data.
